-- ---------------------------------------------------------------- the spectrum, isolated exactly
-- For a Hermitian tridiagonal matrix the leading minors p_k(x) = det(x − T_k) form a Sturm sequence: the number of sign
-- changes in p_0(x), …, p_d(x) is the number of eigenvalues greater than x. At x = n/2^s the fraction-free values
-- Q_k = D_k n Q_{k−1} − N_k D_{k−1} 4^s Q_{k−2} (Q_k = 2^{ks}(Π D) p_k) have the same signs; so each count is d steps of
-- integer arithmetic, and bisection isolates every eigenvalue in an interval of width 2^{−s}, exactly.
sign-step : Bool × (Bool × Nat) → BZ → Bool × (Bool × Nat)
sign-step st x = if bin-zero (snd x) then st else (if fst st then (if bit-eq (fst (snd st)) (fst x) then st else (true , (fst x , suc (snd (snd st))))) else (true , (fst x , snd (snd st))))
